 # Changelog
 
+## 1.6.0
+
+- Ticket assignment. `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee` with `{"assignee": "<agent>"}` assigns an open or in-progress ticket
+  (`{"assignee": null}` unassigns it); the agent is notified (`ticket.assigned`), and each change is audited
+  (`ticket.assigned`, `ticket.unassigned`). `GET /tickets?assignee=<agent>` lists an agent's tickets, `assignee=` the
+  unassigned ones.
+- `ASSIGNEES=on` shows `assignee` on every ticket; until then the tickets look as in 1.5.0, as with `DUE_TIMES`. Roll out
+  in two steps: deploy 1.6.0, then set `ASSIGNEES=on`. The data file stays at version 1 (`assignee` is an optional ticket
+  field); 1.5.0 ignores it and drops assignments at its next save.
+- Fix: a listing with several filters keeps only the tickets that match all of them (it kept those matching any).
+- The command line lists each ticket's assignee: a table column, and a fifth column of `list --raw`, after the title.
+
 ## 1.5.0
 
 - Due times ([decision 9](docs/decisions/0009-due-times.md)). Every ticket gets a due time, `due`: the time it was created
